Subject: [PATCH] diffusion_policy: make PlainConv's global max-pool optional

train_rgbd.py hardcodes PlainConv(pool_feature_map=True), which selects
nn.AdaptiveMaxPool2d((1,1)) and collapses the encoder's 8x8x128 feature map
to a 128-vector before the FC. Every spatial coordinate is discarded; cube
position can only survive as "which channels fired".

On StackCube-v1 that is the binding constraint: under obs-mode rgb the state
vector carries tcp_pose + qpos/qvel and no cube pose (stack_cube.py:135), so
all cube localisation must flow through this encoder. Measured at 100 demos:
corr(cubeA, reach target) 0.69-0.82 with 86 mm mean reach error against a
40 mm cube -- real but coarse tracking, the signature of a position code with
no spatial support.

Exposed as an Args field rather than flipped in place so both arms stay
runnable and the value lands in wandb's config via vars(args). Default False
(spatial map kept); pass --pool_feature_map to reproduce upstream's recipe.

No shape fix is needed on the non-pooled branch: its FC input is written
128*4*4*4 = 8192, which equals 128*8*8 for a 128x128 input. Only the inline
[4,4] shape comments are stale.

--- a/examples/baselines/diffusion_policy/train_rgbd.py
+++ b/examples/baselines/diffusion_policy/train_rgbd.py
@@ -83,6 +83,12 @@
     n_groups: int = (
         8  # jigu says it is better to let each group have at least 8 channels; it seems 4 and 8 are simila
     )
+    pool_feature_map: bool = False
+    """whether the visual encoder global-max-pools its feature map to a single
+    vector per channel. True is upstream's setting and discards all spatial
+    layout; False keeps the 8x8 grid (FC input 8192 instead of 128), which is
+    what a task needs when object position is only available from pixels.
+    Checkpoints are NOT interchangeable across this flag."""
 
     # Environment/experiment specific arguments
     obs_mode: str = "rgb+depth"
@@ -270,7 +276,8 @@
 
         visual_feature_dim = 256
         self.visual_encoder = PlainConv(
-            in_channels=total_visual_channels, out_dim=visual_feature_dim, pool_feature_map=True
+            in_channels=total_visual_channels, out_dim=visual_feature_dim,
+            pool_feature_map=args.pool_feature_map
         )
         self.noise_pred_net = ConditionalUnet1D(
             input_dim=self.act_dim,  # act_horizon is not used (U-Net doesn't care)
